if you were asked to think of the most  important wars in the 20th century you'd  likely think of the world wars Vietnam  or the wars of decolonization it's  unlikely that many people would think of  the three undeclared wars between  Iceland in the United Kingdom which  occurred between 1958 and 1976 these  were the cod Wars and were fought  between the Icelandic Coast Guard and  the Royal Navy and every time Iceland  won there's some nuance to this but to  put it mildly  this was embarrassing for Britain and  does raise the question how on earth did  Iceland defeat the United Kingdom three  times in a row so background British  fishermen have been using the waters  around Iceland for hundreds of years at  this point  as you know Britain's favourite dish  fish and chips required cod and lots of  it and so the British kept taking more  and more and more and more of it given  that Iceland's economy was based around  fishing this led to Icelandic incomes  decreasing by just under 20% and as such  the Icelandic government had to do  something as of the 1950s it was  internationally agreed that all nations  had exclusive use of the waters within  three miles of their coast in 1952  Iceland declared that they would  increase this to four miles and in 1958  they declared that they would further  increase it to twelve Britain decided to  ignore this because nobody else was  doing it and also Iceland was the little  nation with a population of about  170,000 people and so what were they  really going to do about it  well the Icelandic Coast Guard tried to  detain a British fishing trawler but had  to withdraw after the Royal Navy  intervened over the next two years both  sides fired warning shots at each other  but barring that there wasn't a great  deal of action in 1961 Britain climbed  down and agreed to recognise Iceland's  claim of twelve-mile was in return for  rights to fish there during certain  mumps the first Cod war was over but by  1971 Iceland was back to square one with  its fisheries in trouble again British  fishermen flocked to Iceland during the  mumps they were permitted to fish there  which led to depleted stocks and the  same problems as last time as such the  newly elected Icelandic government  declared that it held the exclusive  rights to all fish within 50 miles of  its coastline not only did this upset  Britain but also West Germany who also  had fishermen operating in the area and  Denmark Denmark was involved because it  saw the Icelandic demands as encroaching  on its waters around the Faroe Islands  Kew Cod war - international arbitration  ruled in favour of Britain Germany and  Denmark and Iceland then promptly  ignored it and started firing on British  trawlers and as a result it was time to  get the Royal Navy involved now  obviously this wasn't going to be  traditional naval war British ships  didn't to stop blowing up the Icelandic  Coast Guard instead they were ordered  only to respond to Icelandic ships  firing upon them but this didn't mean  that they couldn't do anything and it  wasn't long until British warships were  ramming Icelandic vessels and vice versa  which in turn led to several casualties  so Britain did have one major problem in  all of this naval e the two nations  weren't even comparable but Iceland had  an ace up its sleeve which was its  relationship to NATO and so does it  threatened to withdraw from NATO if  Britain didn't back down Britain didn't  wish to jeopardize the Alliance or more  specifically annoy the Americans and so  they agreed to recognize the Icelandic  demands this was done on the agreement  that British ships would be allowed to  return after two years and things were  finally sorted that is until the  agreement ran out and British ships  returned Cod war three you know the  drill by now Britain wanted to fish  Iceland said no one subsequently claimed  more exclusive fishing rights this time  200 miles Britain fished anyway the Navy  got involved ramming in 1976 Iceland  broke off international relations with  the UK and after a great deal of  pressure from the US Britain folded its  acknowledged Iceland's economic claims  that see him the two restored relation  soon after the cod wars were finally  over I hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with the special  thanks to my patreon supporters who you  can see on screen here and with an extra  special thanks to James Bissonnette  David archaeologist party-boy Co Danny  Maloney Colin Castleman Rob otter house  are in the white Michael Reynolds H way  an emperor Chris wicker Gustav Swan  Gareth Turner spinning three plates  David Silverman Winston Cawood Maggie  packs Kowski Christian check' Anthony  Beckett Robert Wetzel Skye Chappell and  Ike
 

